		<p class="LRH" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:0;orphans:1;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:center;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin: 10px 0px 10px 0pt; page-break-after: always; border-bottom: 1px solid; margin-top: 10.0pt; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 10.0pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: center; font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: TimesNewRomanPSStd-Regular; color: black;">80</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:left;text-indent:0;widows:2;margin-top:8pt;"><a href="#TOC001">Table of Contents</a></p>



	<div class="_idGenObjectStyleOverride-1" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;border-width:0pt;">
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Revenues</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;"><span class="Bold" style="font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">Sales of products.<span style="width: 13px;display: inline-block;">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span></span>Sales of products represents the sales of high<span class="nobreak">-performance</span> digital asset mining machines to end customers. The revenue of sales of products was $6.9&#160;million and $8.6&#160;million for the&#160;years ended December&#160;31, 2021, and 2022, respectively, increasing by $1.7&#160;million, or 24%. The increase in sales of products revenue was mainly due to the decrease in BTC price in 2022, resulting the decrease in price of the mining machines. The customers are more willing to buy machines in lower price.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;"><span class="Bold" style="font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">Hosting service.<span style="width: 13px;display: inline-block;">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span></span>Hosting service represented the provision of hosting service and daily maintenance of servers to customers. The hosting service revenue decreased by $1.3&#160;million, or 50%, from $2.6&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021 to $1.3&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. Our hosting facilities are mainly based in PRC in 2021, and Kazakhstan in 2022. On May&#160;21, 2021, the Financial Stability and Development Committee of the State Council in China proposed to &#8220;crack down on bitcoin mining and trading.&#8221; We then terminated all the mining business in China, and restart our hosting service in Kazakhstan in second half of 2021. Our hosting service in 2022 was affected largely by Kazakhstan&#8217;s unrest. The hosting service gap&#160;months in 2022 resulted in the decrease in hosting revenue.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;"><span class="Bold" style="font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">Mining Pool.<span style="width: 13px;display: inline-block;">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span></span>Mining pool income represents revenues from the company&#8217;s self<span class="nobreak">-owned</span> sai.plus mining pool which was started in 2021, representing mining rewards from sai.plus mining pool. The Company allocates mining rewards to each pool participant, mainly our hosting clients, net of the pool operator fees based on the sharing mechanism predetermined and records as cost of mining pool revenue. Mining pool revenue decreased by $6.8&#160;million, or 91%, from $7.5&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021 to $0.7&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. In 2021, our hosting customer in PRC participated our sai.plus mining pool for bitcoin mining, however in 2022, our hosting customer switched to other mining pool suppliers, resulting the decrease in our mining pool revenue.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;"><span class="Bold" style="font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">Mining revenue.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>Mining revenue represents mining rewards generated from the company&#8217;s self<span class="nobreak">-owned</span> mining machines. The mining revenue mainly derives from our operation in Mexico starting from 2022.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Cost of revenues</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Cost of revenues primarily included the cost for the purchase of high<span class="nobreak">-performance</span> digital asset mining machines and the direct costs incurred for the provision of hosting service and mining rewards allocated to each provider of pool participant in exchange for their computing power contributed to the mining pool.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">The cost of revenues decreased by $6.3&#160;million or 40%, from $15.8&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021, to $9.5&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. The decrease in cost of revenues was basically in line with the decrease in revenue.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Gross (loss)/profit and gross margin</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Our gross profit decreased by $0.12&#160;million, from $1.26&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021, to gross profit of $1.14&#160;million for year ended December&#160;31, 2022. Gross profit as a percentage of revenue (&#8220;gross margin&#8221;) was 7 % and 11% for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021 and 2022, respectively.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Selling and marketing expenses</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Our selling and marketing expenses primarily consist of salary and benefits expense, advertising expenses, share<span class="nobreak">-based</span> award expenses and travelling expenses to participate in marketing activities. Selling and marketing expenses decreased by $13.7&#160;million from 14.8&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021, to $1.1&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. We made a share<span class="nobreak">-based</span> payment of $14.5&#160;million in 2021 as a result of awarded restricted shares to a consultant for his service of introducing digital asset mining resources providers outside China in 2021, and share<span class="nobreak">-based</span> payment in 2022 was $0.2&#160;million, decreased by $14.3&#160;million. Salary and benefits expense increased $0.24&#160;million and transportation expense increased $0.14&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022, mainly due to our business expansion and increased marketing activities in North America in 2022.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">General and administrative expenses</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Our general and administrative expenses mainly represented salaries and bonus, office related expenses, idle assets depreciation cost and professional service fees. General and administrative expenses increased by $3.70&#160;million, or 155%, from $2.38&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021, to $6.08&#160;million for the </p>
		</div>

		<p class="RRH" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:0;orphans:1;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:center;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin: 10px 0px 10px 0pt; page-break-after: always; border-bottom: 1px solid; margin-top: 10.0pt; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 10.0pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: center; font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: TimesNewRomanPSStd-Regular; color: black;">81</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:left;text-indent:0;widows:2;margin-top:8pt;"><a href="#TOC001">Table of Contents</a></p>



	<div class="_idGenObjectStyleOverride-1" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;border-width:0pt;">
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">year ended December&#160;31, 2022. The increase was mainly attributable to an increase of $2.4&#160;million salary and benefits expenses, from $0.65&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021 to $3.06&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. The increase on one hand, is due to share<span class="nobreak">-based</span> payment expense, which is $0.79&#160;million and nil, respectively, for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022 and 2021, and on the other hand due to the increase in headcount, the general and administrative department employee number increased by 4 in 2022, from 13 members as of January&#160;1, 2022, to 17 members as of December&#160;31, 2022. Depreciation expense increased by $1.18&#160;million. Due to the decrease in BTC price and high market volatility in 2022, the Company shut down most miners and depreciation during the shut<span class="nobreak">-down</span> period is recorded in the general and administrative expenses. We also made impairment test of our miners and equipment regarding the situation, please refer to <span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Impairment of long</span><span class="nobreak"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">-lived</span></span><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;"> assets </span>for more information.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Research and development expenses</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Our research and development expenses mainly represented the cost related to our new product research and development. Research and development expenses increased by $0.06&#160;million, or 14%, from $0.42&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021, to $0.48&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. Salary and benefits expenses increased by $0.06&#160;million, from $0.07&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021 to $0.13&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022. The increase mainly due to the increase in 2022 headcount.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Impairment of long-lived assets</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">The impairment of long<span class="nobreak">-lived</span> assets increased $0.82&#160;million in 2022, or 604%, from $0.14&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021 to $0.95&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Our impairment of long<span class="nobreak">-lived</span> assets in 2022 consists of impairment of cryptocurrencies and impairment of property, plant and equipment. Due to the decrease in BTC price, increasing electricity cost and high market volatility in 2022, the management shut down most of the miners and reviewed the impairment of miners and equipment. We assess the recoverability of the assets based on the undiscounted future cash flows the assets are expected to generate and recognize an impairment loss when estimated undiscounted future cash flows expected to result from the use of the asset plus net proceeds expected from disposition of the asset, if any, are less than the carrying value of the asset. If an impairment is identified, the Company would reduce the carrying amount of the asset to its estimated fair value based on a discounted cash flows approach or, when available and appropriate, to comparable market values. We recognized $0.59&#160;million in mining equipment impairment loss. Impairment of digital assets was $0.06&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022, which was recorded to reflect our cryptocurrencies at the lower of carrying value or fair value as of December&#160;31, 2022.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">Our impairment of long<span class="nobreak">-lived</span> assets in 2021 consists of impairment provided for construction in process, the value of which management determined not recoverable due to changes in the regulatory environment in the PRC.&#160;Impairment of long<span class="nobreak">-lived</span> assets was $0.14&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Other income/(expense), net</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">The other expense was $1.38&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022, mainly comprises of $0.90&#160;million compensation to vendors due to revocation of miners purchase agreements, and $0.72&#160;million loss due to disposal of certain plants and equipment.</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">The other expense was $0.2&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021, mainly relates to the disposal of certain plants and equipment.</p>
		<p class="H4" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:1;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="Italic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Net (loss)/income</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">As a result of the foregoing, we had net loss of $8.85&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022, and net loss of $16.7&#160;million for the year ended December&#160;31, 2021.</p>
		</div>

		<p class="LRH" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:0;orphans:1;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:center;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin: 10px 0px 10px 0pt; page-break-after: always; border-bottom: 1px solid; margin-top: 10.0pt; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 10.0pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: center; font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: TimesNewRomanPSStd-Regular; color: black;">82</p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:left;text-indent:0;widows:2;margin-top:8pt;"><a href="#TOC001">Table of Contents</a></p>



	<div class="_idGenObjectStyleOverride-1" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;border-width:0pt;">
		<p class="H3" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:12pt;orphans:99;page-break-after:avoid;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:1;margin-top:12pt;"><span class="BoldItalic" style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">For the year ended December&#160;31, 2020, and 2021</span></p>
		<p class="Text_flush" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:0;widows:3;margin-top:8pt;">The following table shows key components of our results of operations for the&#160;years ended December&#160;31, 2020, and 2021, in dollars and as a percentage of fluctuations (dollars in thousands).</p>
		<table class="No-Table-Style TableOverride-1" style="width: 100.0%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid #000; border-width: 0pt; margin: 10pt 0 10pt 0;">


				<tr class="No-Table-Style _idGenTableRowColumn-19" style="height:12pt;">
					<td class="TCH" style="border-bottom-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-left-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-top-width:0pt;padding-bottom:4pt;padding-left:3pt;padding-right:3pt;padding-top:2pt;vertical-align:bottom;padding-left:0pt;width: 37.18%; padding: 0in 0in 3px 0in;border-width: 0pt;" valign="bottom">

					</td>
